                        "digest": "sha256:fb7735d19d3cfc5f55e061054965268d49685a1c12498324d990b516c9a3cb3b",
                        "title": "Drop redundant clone and fuse elementwise chain in place (6 kernels -> 4)",
                        "direction": "In run.py, `run(inputs)` no longer builds `torch.relu(x*1.25 + y*0.75 - 0.125)` and then `.clone()`s it. Instead it allocates exactly one fresh output buffer via `torch.mul(inputs['x'], 1.25)`, then applies `out.add_(inputs['y'], alpha=0.75)`, `out.sub_(0.125)`, and returns `torch.relu_(out)`. Kernel count drops from 6 to 4, temporary allocations drop from 4 to 1, and the returned tensor is still a fresh tensor independent of the inputs. Order of arithmetic matches the reference (scale x, scale-add y, subtract bias, relu) so results stay within atol/rtol 1e-5.",
